</figure>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jin et al. (2025b)</a></cite>, content enclosed within <span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#03B6E9;">&lt;search&gt;</span> <span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#03B6E9;">&lt;/search&gt;</span> tags is parsed as the search query, which corresponds to the Action <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>.
The returned search results are then wrapped in <span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#C46F40;">&lt;information&gt;</span> <span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#C46F40;">&lt;/information&gt;</span> tags to form the Observation <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>o</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o</annotation></semantics></math>, thereby completing the ReAct tuple <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tau,\alpha,o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tau,\alpha,o)</annotation></semantics></math>.
The prompt template for each question as:</p>
</div>
